  <div class="body">
    <div class="sponsor"><strong>A note before we start.</strong> This piece references a product I was introduced to last spring, used through a full season, and now recommend. <em>Field &amp; Tackle</em> received product to evaluate. Opinions are mine.</div>

    <p class="lead">I fought ticks the same way for thirty-five seasons — OFF on my arms, permethrin on my pants — and kept getting bit anyway. This is why I made the switch to Pinemoor.</p>

    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>

    <h2><span class="num">Reason 1</span>The old bug spray you've been using might be more dangerous than the ticks</h2>
    <figure class="fig">
      <div class="frame"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1009/5601/2725/files/hf_20260611_220047_c6b954ec-7b98-4613-91bc-5346a08248b6.png?v=1781215545&width=1400" alt="Conventional bug spray versus the ticks it fails to stop." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1400" height="1400"></div>
      <figcaption><strong>35 years in my hunting pack.</strong> Not anymore.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>DEET's been around since 1946 — <strong>a solvent strong enough to melt fishing line.</strong> It rides your exposed skin for a few hours and that's it.</p>
    <p>Permethrin is worse: a pesticide the EPA itself calls <em>"likely to be carcinogenic to humans"</em> — meant for your clothing, <strong>never your skin.</strong></p>
    <p>And the "natural" alternatives? Diluted almost beyond usefulness — some carrying <strong>the same warning language you find on a cigarette package.</strong></p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">See What I Replaced It With</a></div>

    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>

    <h2><span class="num">Reason 2</span>Ticks hunt by questing. Pinemoor blocks this process completely.</h2>
    <figure class="fig">
      <div class="frame"><img src="{{ 'pm-ezgif-com-video-to-gif-e7b22.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="A tick questing, front legs extended, waiting for a host." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="600" height="450"></div>
      <figcaption><strong>Questing.</strong> Front legs out, reading the CO₂ you breathe, your body heat, and the ammonia and lactic acid in your sweat. Host or pass — decided in under a second.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>A tick is blind. It reads three signals: the CO₂ you breathe, your body heat, and the lactic acid in your sweat.</p>
    <p>Think of your body like a candle in a dark room — your heat is the flame, your scent is the smoke. The tick waits in the grass to feel that candle go by.</p>
    <p>Sprays don't blow out the candle. They make one patch of you smell bad, so the tick crawls past it to your hairline, your waistband, or <em>the back of your knee.</em></p>
    <p><strong>Pinemoor changes the scent coming off your entire body — the quest comes up empty.</strong></p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">Stop Smelling Like A Host</a></div>

    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>

    <h2><span class="num">Reason 3</span>Taken internally, it builds a chemical barrier that changes your scent profile</h2>
    <figure class="fig">
      <div class="frame"><video src="https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/a9065e15010845ebb0eb10a19855f75d.mp4?width=1400" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video></div>
    </figure>
    <p>This is where Pinemoor beats anything you can spray on.</p>
    <p>Because you take it internally, the herbal compounds circulate and get expressed through your skin's natural oils and sweat — building a <strong>whole-body chemical barrier that alters your scent profile</strong>. That tick signaling I was explaining from Reason 2? It now says <em>undesirable host</em> — everywhere a tick can crawl, no patch left uncovered.</p>
    <p>And the barrier bites back: the carvacrol in oregano has demonstrated the ability to <strong>kill ticks on contact</strong> — something no spray is capable of — along with documented antimicrobial, antioxidant, and anti-inflammatory properties.</p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">Change What Ticks Smell</a></div>

    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>

    <h2><span class="num">Reason 4</span>These herbal compounds have been proven to work for thousands of years</h2>
    <figure class="fig">
      <div class="frame"><img src="{{ 'pm-yell-10115-b1f2d.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Historical photograph of life in tick country." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="938" height="584"></div>
    </figure>
    <p>Native Americans lived, hunted, and raised their families in the heaviest tick country on this continent for thousands of years — and <strong>ticks never decimated their populations.</strong> They ate these same concentrated herbs before heading into the woods, and the ticks left them alone.</p>
    <p><strong>Pinemoor was built off those foundational principles</strong> — the recipe fine-tuned, the concentrations matched to modern research, and the whole thing carried in pure maple syrup so it actually tastes good going down.</p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">The Old Way, Done Right</a></div>

